From 69a6d1c4e78f998388f804fd879f214e62f5fe68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:41:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 251/348] Unified: a step in the same window, not another mode
 (sketch, tool panels)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

While a sketch is drawn or a tool's panel is open, a band below the tool
strip says what is being done ("Drawing the sketch …", "Working on …"),
with "✓ Done" and "✕ Cancel" (one pair: the panel's own OK and Cancel are
hidden) and, for a sketch, its tools by name (line, rectangle, circle, arc,
polygon, dimension, the main constraints, trim, extend, fillet, external
geometry, and "More" for the rest). Sketcher's toolbars are not shown;
their shortcuts keep working. The tool strip, the history and the search
stay where they are. Cancel goes back to before the step, also for a
sketch (what was drawn is undone). A tool of the strip pressed during a
step finishes the step first and then starts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
